      "text": "Gene mutations in either the *BRCA1* or the *BRCA2* genes are responsible for the majority of hereditary breast cancer in humans."
    },
    {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "The proteins produced by the two genes migrate to the nucleus where they interact with other proteins, such as those produced by the tumour suppressor gene, *p53*, and the DNA repair gene, *RAD51*."
    },
